 The Clustal parsers in ``Bio.AlignIO`` and ``Bio.Align`` now accept files whose
 header line starts with ``CLUSTALW`` as a single word, as written by some tools.
 
+The ``BgzfWriter`` in ``Bio.bgzf`` can now write data which does not compress
+(e.g. random or already compressed data), which previously failed with a
+``struct.error`` or ``RuntimeError``. Such data is split into smaller blocks.
